<ScenContainer xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <ScenTitle>Advanced ASW Exercise, 1979</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Paul Bridge&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 30 October 1979&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; English Channel&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; FOST Units &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 24 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Flag Officer Sea Training (FOST) is a Royal Navy training organisation responsible for training Royal Navy and Royal Fleet Auxiliary vessels so that they are fit to join the operational fleet. FOST puts crews and vessels through rigorous exercises and readiness inspections that can last up to eight weeks to prepare them for any eventuality. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;One of the final assessments is protection of a high-value unit en route to rendezvous in the face of enemy submarine attack. Are you up to the challenge? &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
